WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.067
-Our next guest is a Tony
and Emmy Award-winning actress

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.834
you know from shows
such as "The West Wing"

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:07.133
and "Pushing Daisies"
and from Broadway productions

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:09.934
like "Wicked" and
"On the 20th Century."

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:12.501
She stars in the second
season of "Schmigadoon!",

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:15.133
which premieres
Wednesdays on Apple TV+.

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.834
Please welcome back to the show
our friend Kristin Chenoweth.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:20.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:28.968
♪♪

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:37.167
♪♪

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:41.067
You -- I mean, your
very personality sparkles,

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:43.868
but for you to also wear
an outfit that does...

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.300
-Listen.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.334
I'm showing up
for the Seth Meyers show, okay?

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.133
I see you didn't.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.133
-You know I love you.
-How dare you? How dare you?

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:55.701
I would look ridiculous
in your outfit.

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:58.100
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.601
-This is --
This is a wonderful show.

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.200
We've talked about
the first season with you

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.801
over the years --
And not over the years,

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:05.601
but the second season --
and the first year

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.000
that you did this show
was very difficult.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.300
It was in the middle of COVID,
hard core protocols.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.534
-Yes. We wore cones like dogs.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:15.434
It was very unfair to make
a star like you wear a cone.

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:17.334
-I know.
I was like, "Sit? Okay.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.033
Eat? Alright."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.901
That's what it felt like.
Sorry.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:23.734
-And you -- you were
right across the hall

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.868
in a hotel from your friend
and costar, Alan Cumming.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:27.067
-Yes.
-But this year,

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.667
a bit of an upgrade --
not over Alan,

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.834
but over the living arrangement.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:32.968
-You shared a home
with Cecily Strong.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:37.234
-Yeah, so I was in the Sutton,
this -- our hotel.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:40.100
I call it the "Slutton."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.734
-This is a -- Let's go a little
deeper on the Slutton.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:45.701
This is -- This
is a hotel in Vancouver

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:46.834
that everybody --
-You who know it well.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.100
-I know it.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.133
Everybody who's working
on a production up there,

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.400
of which there are many --
-We all stay there.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.200
-And they all show up
in the hotel bar.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.501
-Yeah. And we all do the bar,
and we all do the workout

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:57.767
and we call it the Slutton.

00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:00.234
And I think it's because
people act like sluts there.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.934
-Yeah.
-I'm not sure it does.

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:03.334
-Like, I feel like
of the places

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:06.400
I've been in my life,
"what happens here, stays here"

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.300
was far truer of the
Slutton than it is of Las Vegas.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.667
-Absolutely, baby.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.167
-So, yeah.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:17.367
So I lived next door to Alan
in the Slutton -- Sutton and...

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:20.434
and this year I was upset

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:23.133
because my dog -- there was
an issue with my dog.

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.400
Anyway, Cecily said, "You want
to come live with me?"

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:30.300
And I'm like, "Absolutely,"
because she is like me.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.334
We're both bat [bleep],
but we love each other.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:35.067
[ Laughter ]
-Dog lovers as well.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:37.400
-I mean, her dog is like my dog.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.400
I just --
I loved living with her.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.167
She said it was a little
"Flowers in the Attic."

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:44.200
She said, "You can stay
in the basement."

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:48.467
So I lived down there.
There was a gym, not that --

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.067
neither one of us
ever touched it,

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:54.501
but there was a gym
and there was no light.

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:56.601
I'm one of those sleepers
that likes to sleep

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.767
with not one little
piece of light.

00:02:58.767 --> 00:02:59.834
There was no light.

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:01.701
And I literally
was like a vampire.

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:04.734
I would -- I was upside
down asleep every night.

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:07.567
And she would -- I would come up
in the mornings and she'd go,

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:09.801
"You're a real va--
like, you're a bat."

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:11.100
Like, "I know."

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.200
We would watch all of our shows.
-So you have --

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.167
That's very important.

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:17.300
You have similar
tastes in shows?

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.667
-Have you met her?
-Yeah, I have.

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:22.968
-Okay. So we both love the
housewives of any county.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:26.067
-Okay. You're not picky.
-Not picky.

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.434
And we were obsessed
with the Salt Lake City.

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:30.467
Uh-huh.
Yeah, there was --

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.100
There was some criminal
activity, right?

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.334
-Do you know what's going on?

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:36.701
-I only know
there's maybe been some arrests.

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:39.033
-Yes, Seth.
-It's very fun.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:41.634
I have this very nice thing
where I'm just on the outside

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.834
of understanding
anything in that world,

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:46.567
but I appreciate that
if I get in, I'll never get out.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.234
-You'll never get out.

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:50.067
-They say it's like
going in Cecily's basement.

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:51.734
Once you're there...
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:54.601
You never come out!
So we would get this --

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:58.467
She said, "I have this vodka
and it's organic."

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.667
I was like,
"I'm all -- That's good.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.501
Organic vodka."
-I did not know

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:04.334
they all weren't.
-I -- [ Laughs ]

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.300
Because, right?
-Yeah.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.133
-How do you make --
How do you -- That...?

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:10.934
-It feels like they've all
been wiped with an alcohol swab.

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:12.601
-It's one big alcohol.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:14.868
-So anyway, we'd sit there
and we watch --

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.400
So first of all,
I love the housewives.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.133
They make me feel better
about my own life.

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:21.033
-Uh-huh.
-And I've actually become

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.400
friends with a couple of them.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.534
If you like "Housewives
of Salt Lake City" like I do,

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:28.367
Heather Gay has a wonderful
book called "Bad Mormon."

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.434
You should read it.

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:32.100
And it's not about
Heather, is it?

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:35.601
Anyway, back to me.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.367
She -- She's
a delightful person.

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:39.367
But there's this girl
on there named Jen Shah,

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:40.834
and I know some of you ladies

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.067
and probably some of you men
know what I'm talking about.

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:44.601
She actually stole --

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:47.000
she accidentally stole
from old people.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.667
[ Laughter ]
-She accidentally --

00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.634
She sound like one
of Donald Trump's lawyers.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:53.767
[ Laughter ]
-By the way,

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:55.601
you're Lindsey Graham
and Donald Trump

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.901
can be Tony Award-worthy.
-Thank you very much!

00:04:57.901 --> 00:05:00.100
And you have a Tony,
so that means a lot.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.567
I will ask for a quote
for you for the poster.

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:04.501
-Done. I mean, it was good.

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:07.601
-Wait, what about -- It seems
like there's a lot happening

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:10.133
in the world of the Vanderpumps.
-Oh!

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:11.801
Oh.
-Okay.

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:14.367
So again, I sort of, you know,
a headline --

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:15.834
as a headline spotter only,

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:17.534
I realize there's
sort of a storm brewing.

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:18.567
Is this something
we should all try

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:19.868
to engage ourselves
in this story?

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.634
Is it worth...?
-Well, if you like yourself.

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.434
-Okay, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:27.601
-There is a long-term
couple on their named

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:30.300
Tom and named Ariana.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.133
Now I'm fixing to get a shirt
that says Team Ariana.

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:34.534
-Okay, gotcha.
-I did

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:35.501
"Watch What Happens Live."

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.434
I've probably done that...

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:37.534
Andy's a good friend of mine.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:38.901
I've done that show a lot
because I am --

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:42.200
I know the Bravo shows,
like "Married at First Sight."

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.000
Come on, that's a car wreck
waiting to happ--

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.767
I just love it.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:48.367
Anyway, they broke up

00:05:48.367 --> 00:05:51.434
because her good friend
is cheating with Tom.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:52.868
-Oh, my goodness.
-And I did "Watch What Happens"

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:55.200
with him, and he always seemed
a little smarmy to me.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.968
And there you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.968 --> 00:05:58.133
-Alright. Well, you know what?

00:05:58.133 --> 00:05:59.767
I don't know anything,
but Team Ariana as well.

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:00.767
-Yes!
-I'm jumping on.

00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:01.801
-Thank you.
-I'm with you.

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:02.901
I have a bunch more to ask you.

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:04.200
We'll be right back with more

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.467
from my friend
Kristin Chenoweth.

